    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required rejecting owner creation with HTTP 429 once 100+ owners have already been created today (by `registrationDate`).\n\nI added a single new, self-contained class: `OwnerDailyLimitAdvice.java`. It follows the exact pattern of the existing `OwnerCityCapacityAdvice` \u2014 a `RequestBodyAdvice` `@ControllerAdvice` that:\n\n- Intercepts only the `addOwner` create endpoint (via `supports`).\n- In `afterBodyRead`, counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws a small exception when the count reaches 100.\n- Maps that exception to `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` via an `@ExceptionHandler`.\n\n**Structural impact:** zero existing methods or classes were modified \u2014 the behaviour lives entirely in one new file with small, cohesive methods each carrying near-zero surrounding complexity (`WMC_other`). The full test suite, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit`, passes.",
